      "name": "Rattling Bolt",
      "itemType": "ammunition",
      "level": 4,
      "rarity": "uncommon",
      "traits": [
        "arcane",
        "consumable",
        "magical"
      ],
      "description": "Ammunition bolts\nActivate 1 Interact\nSometimes when dealing with undead incursions, a more subtle approach is called for. Paradoxically, this is precisely what the rattling bolts are most often used for, despite each one ringing like a shaken chain when launched. Once it hits the target, the rattling transfers into that creature's body. A target damaged by the rattling bolt must succeed at a check (fortitude, dc:25) save or be Deafened and Stupefied 1 for 1 round (or 1 minute on a critical hit). An undead affected by a rattling bolt further loses any lifesense ability it might have had for the same duration as the deafening.",
